Purpose: Answer :visited per container. Places records the container of every visit but answers :visited for the whole profile, and tells every content process about a new visit. With the new pref places.history.isolate_by_user_context (default false, so Firefox is unchanged) the parent asks Places once per container for the processes that host it (the container comes from the requesting process's remote type, never from the request), the SQL only counts visits with that userContextId, and a new visit notifies only the processes of its container. Upstreamable: partly, as a pref-gated feature; the container-aware lookup is small and self-contained.
Test: MOZCONFIG=swell/mozconfig ./mach test swell/tests/app/isolation/browser/browser_history.js --headless

